build/
# Every other build tree too: build.ps1 -Dev writes build-dev/, and a session
# that compares two configurations invents its own (build-demo/, build-rig/...).
# None of them are ever tracked, and an unignored one is ~1300 artifacts that a
# `git add -A` will happily stage. Checked against `git ls-files | grep build`:
# no tracked path starts with "build-", and build.ps1/build.sh/build.cmd are
# files, which this pattern (directories only) cannot match.
build-*/
.vs/
*.user
imgui.ini

# PS2 network-deploy tools, fetched by setup.ps1 (ps2client)...
tools/*
# ...except the reproducible Foot IK trainer and its labelled PCSX2 samples.
!tools/train-foot-neural.py
!tools/data/
tools/data/*
!tools/data/foot-neural-real.csv
!tools/ps2client/
tools/ps2client/*
!tools/ps2client/bin/
tools/ps2client/bin/*
# ...except the patched ps2client (TCP_NODELAY - see tools/ps2client/README.md;
# without it host: file serving to a real console runs at ~4 KB/s)
!tools/ps2client/bin/ps2client.exe
!tools/ps2client/nodelay.patch
!tools/ps2client/README.md
# ...and the SPU silencer used by Stop on PS2 (source + prebuilt ELF; see
# tools/silencer/Makefile - it builds inside the toolchain container)
!tools/silencer/
tools/silencer/*
!tools/silencer/main.c
!tools/silencer/Makefile
!tools/silencer/silencer.elf
# ...and the TyraX ps2link, the only ps2link this editor deploys to (patch +
# build scripts only; the scripts clone ps2link and build the elf, which stays
# ignored - see tools/ps2link/README.md and docs/ps2link-setup.md).
!tools/ps2link/
tools/ps2link/*
!tools/ps2link/README.md
!tools/ps2link/build.ps1
!tools/ps2link/build.sh
!tools/ps2link/tyrax.patch
# ...plus the host harness for the host: protocol code (its own .gitignore drops
# the compiled binary and the pristine-upstream scratch copy).
!tools/ps2link/test/
!tools/ps2link/test/.gitignore
!tools/ps2link/test/run.ps1
!tools/ps2link/test/run.sh
!tools/ps2link/test/test_net_fio.c
!tools/ps2link/test/shim/
!tools/ps2link/test/shim/*.h
# ...and the VS Code extension for .flownode/.screenfx files (see
# tools/vscode-tyrax/README.md; its own .gitignore drops *.vsix + node_modules).
!tools/vscode-tyrax/

# Vendored dependencies are fetched separately (see README)...
vendor/*
# ...except the Tyra engine, which is maintained in-tree: the editor edits
# it directly and syncs it into the build container (Apache License 2.0,
# forked from github.com/h4570/tyra @ 9273416).
!vendor/tyra/
vendor/tyra/*
!vendor/tyra/engine/
!vendor/tyra/Makefile.base
!vendor/tyra/README.MD
# Apache-2.0 section 4 requires the license text to travel with the sources, and
# the engine sources ARE redistributed here. Upstream's own LICENSE was deleted
# by accident in h4570/tyra@44c1ee4 ("remove tyrav1 stuff", 2022) and never
# restored, so this copy is recovered verbatim from h4570/tyra@68eb496 - the
# last commit that had it. See THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md.
!vendor/tyra/LICENSE
# ...and the audsrv fork, which is maintained in-tree the same way: sources
# plus the built module that gets overlaid onto the container's PS2SDK at build
# time (LGPL v2 - see vendor/tyra/audsrv/README.md).
!vendor/tyra/audsrv/
# ...but not its build work tree: a pinned ps2sdk clone the build script
# overlays our sources onto. The sources and the built module are committed;
# that scratch clone is not.
vendor/tyra/audsrv/.work/
vendor/tyra/engine/obj/
vendor/tyra/engine/bin/

# Example projects are ordinary generated projects, and running one drops the
# devkit channel files (livedbg.bin, livetime.bin, livelink.*, log.txt...) into
# its bin/. Each project ships its own .gitignore for that, but a project whose
# build output was committed BEFORE it had one keeps leaking - so this is the
# net at the repo level. All four are build output or local state, and the
# project template declares them ignorable too (TPL_GITIGNORE in templates.cpp).
examples/*/bin/
examples/*/obj/
examples/*/.res-baked/*
# ...except the baked global-illumination cache, which is NOT build output:
# nothing regenerates it but an explicit bake (docs/global-illumination.md), so
# an example that ships GI has to ship the bake or a fresh clone would build it
# with the lighting silently switched off.
!examples/*/.res-baked/gi/
examples/*/*.history

# The same devkit channel files, but dropped in the REPO ROOT: they land here
# whenever the editor or the Live Debugger is run with the repo as its working
# directory, which is what a headless CLI invocation does. Root-anchored, so a
# project that legitimately tracks one is unaffected. livedbg.bin was committed
# by accident before this rule existed and is untracked in the same commit.
/live*.bin
/livelink.*
/vucap.bin
/crash.txt
